Subject: [PATCH v2 1/2] notmuch: Tag messages under archive/ as archived
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Change-Id: stkvtnvrmywyxwmxzqnrxowmrytruwow

A thread on the list never closes on its own. Someone always has the
last word, so the other side keeps an inbox message that needs no
answer: a patch applied without a reply, a question already settled.
Replying just to clear the inbox adds noise and moves the open message
to the other side.

When the moderator files a message's file, unchanged, into the shared
archive/ maildir, it closes for everyone. Because the tag comes from
where the file lives, it lives in the mail branch like every other
derived tag. A rebuilt database gets it back from notmuch new alone,
and moving the file back out undoes it.
---
change-id: stkvtnvrmywyxwmxzqnrxowmrytruwow

 dotfiles/notmuch/hooks/mail-tag.sh | 14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dotfiles/notmuch/hooks/mail-tag.sh b/dotfiles/notmuch/hooks/mail-tag.sh
index 269caaf..44ef44e 100755
--- a/dotfiles/notmuch/hooks/mail-tag.sh
+++ b/dotfiles/notmuch/hooks/mail-tag.sh
@@ -2,16 +2,19 @@
 #
 # mail-tag.sh -- derive notmuch tags from the contents of the list.
 #
-# The sent, inbox and replied tags are recomputed from the messages on
-# every run, so the database holds no state of its own: rebuild it from
-# the maildir and the same tags come back.
+# The sent, inbox, replied and archived tags are recomputed from the
+# messages on every run, so the database holds no state of its own:
+# rebuild it from the maildir and the same tags come back.
 #
 #   sent     from the user (notmuch user.primary_email or other_email)
 #   inbox    from someone else, and the user has not replied to it
 #   replied  from someone else, and the user has replied to it
+#   archived filed under archive/ by the moderator; never in the inbox
 #
 # "Replied to" means a message from the user names it in In-Reply-To.
-# Drafts get none of these tags.
+# The moderator archives by moving a message's file, unchanged, into
+# the shared archive/ maildir, and moving it back undoes it.  Drafts
+# get none of these tags.
 #
 # Runs from the notmuch post-new hook, so notmuch new applies it.
 
@@ -19,6 +22,7 @@ set -eu
 set -o pipefail
 
 readonly drafts='path:drafts/**'
+readonly archive='path:archive/**'
 
 main() {
 	local me id
@@ -31,6 +35,8 @@ main() {
 		replied_ids "${me}" | while read -r id; do
 			echo "+replied -inbox -- id:\"${id}\" and not (${me}) and not ${drafts}"
 		done
+		echo "-archived -- not ${archive}"
+		echo "+archived -inbox -- ${archive}"
 	} | notmuch tag --batch
 }
 
